From df50bb7015740fdb0f0e28ab55278d90a30c7dcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Figueiredo <alex.fernandesfigueiredo@windriver.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:12:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 74/75] Fix watcher decision-engine and add pod tolerations

The upstream watcher chart has three problems on its decision engine
and one on every pod:
- the decision-engine StatefulSet reads .Values.pod.replicas.engine,
  while values.yaml declares pod.replicas.decision_engine, so it always
  runs a single replica;
- the same StatefulSet resolves its entrypoint dependencies from the
  "decision-engine" key, while values.yaml only defines
  dependencies.static.decision_engine, so its init container waits for
  nothing and, on a first install, the decision engine starts before
  the database schema exists and restarts until db-sync completes;
- its pod template lacks the configmap-bin-hash and configmap-etc-hash
  annotations that the API and applier carry, so a configuration
  change does not roll the decision-engine pods;
- no watcher pod or job renders tolerations, so they cannot be
  scheduled on tainted controllers.

Point the StatefulSet at the documented replica and dependency keys,
add the two hash annotations, and add pod.tolerations.watcher (disabled
by default) rendered by the API, applier, decision engine, test pod
and every job, as in aodh.

The replica and dependency key fixes are already merged upstream [1].
The hash annotations and tolerations are proposed upstream in [2]: drop
this patch once the chart is rebased on a revision that includes [2].
Upstream names the etc hash secret-etc-hash, after its rename of
configmap-etc.yaml, and defaults the toleration list to the
control-plane key only. Neither affects stx-openstack, whose static
overrides set the full toleration list.

[1] https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/openstack-helm/+/1011020
[2] https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/openstack-helm/+/1014897

Signed-off-by: Alex Figueiredo <alex.fernandesfigueiredo@windriver.com>
